ABSTRACT

Agriculture —- Announcement made by Hon’ble Chief Minister on 1.6.2016 for Kuruvai

Cultivation Package 2016 in Delta Districts - Sanction of funds — Orders — Issued. Agriculture (AP2) Department

G.O.(Ms).No.155. Dated: 4.6.2016. HGauciEHoit 9, 601) 2047 snus 22 . Read:

1. Announcement made by Hon'ble Chief Minister on 1.6.2016. 2. From the Commissioner of Agriculture letter No.PM1/52431/2016, dated 1.6.2016.

kk

ORDER:

After reviewing the poor storage in the Mettur Dam, the Hon’ble Chief Minister on 1.6.2016 has announced the Kuruvai Cultivation Package Assistance to six delta districts for the year 2016 at a total outlay of Rs.5465.00 lakh. The package involves-

12 hours three phase power supply to six delta districts;

Promotion of Mechanical transplantation;

Distribution of water conveyance pipes;

Distribution of Productivity enhancing inputs;

Encouraging pulses cultivation in Cauvery basin/ grand anaicut canal sub-basin; and

Package for Vennar Region;

Vv VVVWWV

2. Based on the above announcement of Hon’ble Chief Minister, the Commissioner of Agriculture has sent proposals for Kuruvai Cultivation Package 2016 for the six Cauvery delta districts namely Thanjavur, Thiruvarur, Nagapattinam and part of Trichy, Ariyalur and Cuddalore and requested the Government Orders on the following:-

To sanction a total amount of Rs.5465.00 lakh (Rs.2732.50 lakh under National Agriculture Development Programme and Rs.2732.50 lakh from State fund) for implementation of Kuruvai Package assistance in six districts of Cauvery Delta during 2016-2017 as announced by the Hon’ble Chief Minister on 1.6.2016 and also to utilize the savings under above components if any, for covering additional area under this scheme;

Pending provision of such funds in the Revised Estimate / Final Modified Appropriation, 2016-2017, the Commissioner of Agriculture and Chief Engineer (Agricultural Engineering) shall be authorized to draw a sum of Rs.5265.00 lakh and Rs.200.00 lakh respectively and incur the expenditure under various heads of account ;

The Commissioner of Agriculture and Chief Engineer, Agricultural Engineering Department to follow tender procedures as per Tamil Nadu Transparency in Tenders Act and Rules wherever necessary.

2

To authorize Executive Director, Tamil Nadu Watershed Development Agency (TAWDEVA) to draw a sum of Rs.14.35 lakh from the account maintained for the National Agriculture Development Programme Administrative funds and disburse to Commissioner of Agriculture for publicity, documentation and advertisement for floating tenders; and

The Commissioner of Agriculture shall issue detailed guidelines for the scheme implementation;

3. The Government after careful consideration, accept the proposal of Commissioner of Agriculture and accordingly sanction a sum of Rs.5465.00 lakh (Rupees Fifty Four Crore Sixty Five lakh only) (Rs.2732.50 lakh under National Agriculture Development Programme and Rs.2732.50 lakh from State fund) for implementation of Kuruvai Package assistance in six districts of Cauvery Delta during 2016-2017 as detailed in Annexure to this order and the Commissioner of Agriculture is also permitted to utilize a sum of Rs.14.35 lakh (Rupees Fourteen Lakh Thirty Five Thousand only) from National Agriculture Development Programme Administrative funds available with Tamil Nadu Watershed Development Agency towards publicity, documentation and advertisement charges for floating tenders, strictly adhering to the guidelines for implementation of this package.
